  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "0iV7a9gRmBKFrl7lpCs+G0AXG4Y=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:39.742Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "```ts\nexport type UpgradeTransition = {\n  toVersion: number;\n  upgradeReducer: UpgradeReducer<any, any>;   // (document, action) => PHDocument<TTo>\n  description?: string;\n};\n\nexport type UpgradeManifest<TVersions extends readonly number[]> = {\n  documentType: string;\n  latestVersion: TupleMember<TVersions>;   // 1 | 2 | 3\n  supportedVersions: TVersions;            // [1, 2, 3]\n  upgrades: { [V in Exclude<TupleMember<TVersions>, 1> as `v${V}`]: UpgradeTransition };\n};\n```\n\n`TVersions` is passed as a `readonly number[]` tuple (`as const`), and the mapped type **forces an `upgrades` key for every supported version except `1`** \u2014 a manifest for `[1, 2, 3]` requires `v2` and `v3`, and there is no `v1` key because v1 is the base. A manifest with only v1 therefore has `upgrades: {}`. Registry methods type it loosely as `UpgradeManifest<readonly number[]>`.\n\nTwo things that catch people:\n\n- **The registry does not cross-check.** Registering a manifest whose `supportedVersions` do not match the registered module versions **succeeds** \u2014 so a manifest can promise a v3 that no module provides, and the failure appears later at `computeUpgradePath`.\n- **Manifests are codegen output** carrying a `WARNING: DO NOT EDIT` header. You author them by adding versions and upgrade reducers through codegen, across three files: `versions.ts` (`export const supportedVersions = [1, 2] as const`), one transition file per step (`v2.ts` exporting an `UpgradeTransition`), and `upgrade-manifest.ts` assembling them.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/06-DocumentModelRegistry.md` \u2014 Version upgrades \u203a Upgrade types; Authoring a manifest\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:48:39.742Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:39.742Z"
    }
  },
